   "key": "func RawRRBackup.reconcileIndexWithFiles()",
   "hash": "64e4b1149c1b2d47",
   "does": "On appendQueue (reconcileIndexInBackground at init; tests call it directly). Does nothing while the launch read of the index failed. Otherwise builds rows (entriesOnDisk) for backups on disk whose id is neither in the index nor deleted forever by the user (forgottenBackupIds): a first append killed before its index save, a one-shot write killed before its row, or every backup when the index file is missing. Rows are unarchived; an id in the Trash is listed again and shows in the Trash. Under indexLock appends those still unlisted, logs at .warning and saves the index (a failed save is logged; the rows stay in memory for the next save).",
